\title{Universal quantifier (#{\forall})}
\date{2026-02-03T22:22:36Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{The first quantifier we will learn about is the \em{universal} quantifier, which lets us encode the idea behind English words like "all", "every", and "each", that is, \em{universal} statements that are supposed to be true for every member of some domain.}

